    {
      "hunk": 1,
      "file": "src/cdk/bidi/dir.ts",
      "header": "@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ export class Dir implements Directionality, AfterContentInit, OnDestroy {",
      "judgment": "The raw field gains an empty-string initializer to satisfy strict property initialization. Both exact minimum complete public modules contain it; the original module diagnostic distinguishes undefined from empty and rejects the current-field reversion. Owned legacy sources do not import or read this implementation field. Packed public binding/host observations are required but do not pretend to observe the constructor-private before-input state."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 2,
      "file": "src/cdk/bidi/directionality.spec.ts",
      "header": "@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ class InjectsDirectionality {",
      "judgment": "The dynamic-direction test ViewChild field gains a definite-assignment assertion. Angular populates the query before its use; there is no emitted runtime operation or historical component API to mirror."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 3,
      "file": "src/cdk/bidi/directionality.spec.ts",
      "header": "@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@ class ElementWithDir {",
      "judgment": "The predefined-auto test ViewChild field gains the same compile-only assertion. Keep this hunk in the complete individual review without expanding the actual packed case to claim private initialization or every locale."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 4,
      "file": "src/cdk/bidi/directionality.spec.ts",
      "header": "@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ class ElementWithPredefinedAutoDir {",
      "judgment": "The predefined-uppercase test ViewChild field gains the compile-only assertion. The actual packed public uppercase/invalid/empty updates remain separately mandatory, with real output suppression and completion."
    }
  ],
  "source_conclusion": "Inherit the complete strict-initialization change in the maintained public Dir implementation. The original16 raw field starts undefined; both exact minimum public peers initialize it to an empty string. This is current CDK infrastructure, and the add-on neither reads that private before-first-input field nor owns a copy of the directive. The three upstream ViewChild definite-assignment hunks are fixture compile annotations, not legacy API changes. Prior complete original/current dev-and-production namespace diagnostics explicitly observe the initial field and reject reverting it, but that private observation is not attributed to the packed fixture. The required isolated packed case instead proves public normalized values, raw DOM host attributes, real nearest Directionality identities, output ordering/repeat suppression and teardown after actual bindings through the legacy module exports. Require the complete same-run current clean full106 packed artifact execution; source-only or marker-only receipts cannot admit this inherited decision. No CDK fork, consumer HTML/CSS/SCSS change, private product dependency or peer-floor increase is introduced. Complete runtime/compiler/RxJS floors, other callers and G11 remain pending independently.",
